    "name": {
      "value": "Beastmaster'S Sigil"
    },
    "source": {
      "value": "tv"
    },
    "description": {
      "value": "This silver disc displays an ever-changing etching of an animal. When you affix the beastmaster's sigil, the animal settles into a single form based on where you affix it, showing the animal the item can summon when affixed that way. The spell DC of any spell cast by activating this item is 19. A weapon can benefit from only the melee weapon benefit or ranged weapon benefit. A thrown melee weapon gets the melee weapon benefit, and a combination weapon gets only one benefit, which you choose when you affix the spellheart. If it's unclear which one should apply, the GM decides. The sigil grants you a +1 item bonus to saving throws against poison. The sigil grants you a +1 item bonus to Athletics checks to Trip. If you critically hit with the affixed weapon, and the target is adjacent to a creature summoned with the sigil, the target takes 1d6 persistent bleed damage. You cast tame. You cast 2nd-level summon animal to summon a cave scorpion (armor), wolf (melee weapon), or bat swarm (ranged weapon)."
    },
